<p>Corpus Christi flood damage claims usually come from one of two sources: storm surge pushing water across Corpus Christi Bay, Nueces Bay, the barrier islands, and low-lying shorelines, or heavy rain overwhelming streets and drainage inland. Both can leave slab-on-grade homes, garages, and ground-floor businesses with soaked drywall, flooring, cabinets, and contents. This page explains how flood coverage generally works for property owners in Corpus Christi, Nueces County, and the Coastal Bend, where flood claims tend to get complicated, and how a public adjuster can help with the documentation. Flood claims have their own rules, and we try to be clear about what a public adjuster can and cannot do.</p>

<h2>How Flood Coverage Works for Corpus Christi Flood Damage Claims</h2>
<p>Standard homeowners and commercial property policies generally exclude flood, and TWIA windstorm policies cover wind and hail only. That leaves two main sources of flood coverage:</p>
<table>
